<title>GERMANY: German sugar industry opposes storage refund cuts.</title>
<headline>German sugar industry opposes storage refund cuts.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sugar industry association WVZ will oppose plans by the European Commission to reduce the 1997/98 (July/June) monthly sugar storage refund, it said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>WVZ said the proposed cut by 17 percent to 0.35 Ecus per 100 kg followed reductions by 33 percent over the last three years.</p>
<p>EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler had failed to take advantage of the EU's financial reserves in order to adjust the refunds to a level which would compensate store holders for their costs, it said.</p>
<p>WVZ called on the council of EU farm ministers, which meets March 17-18, to implement a financially reliable sugar storage policy with producer interests in mind.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
